    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30608" root="عمه" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْمَهُ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمِهٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [Its fem.] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمْهَآءُ</span>, applied to
a land (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ</span>), signifies <i>Having in it no signs of
the way</i> (S, Msb, K) <i>to guide to safety.</i> (Msb.)
[Hence, accord. to the Msb, the verb <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمِهَ</span> expl.
above: but some hold it to be tropical: see 1,
last sentence.]

